<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training with FAQ-IT.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation study of BenchIT fine-tuning on LLaVA-NeXT and Qwen2.5-VL models across our benchmark levels. VE denotes Vision Encoder. The symbol <math id="S4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a zero-shot scenario where the model has not been trained. Symbol <math id="S4.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{FAQ-IT^{\spadesuit}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♠</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{FAQ-IT^{\spadesuit}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{FAQ-IT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{FAQ-IT}</annotation></semantics></math> means training models on static-only QA from FAQ and training on full FAQ, respectively.</span></figcaption>
